Do not detect memfd_create through meson's has_function(): DeskDroid builds
for API 29 and memfd_create is API 30+, so vtest_shm.c falls back to ashmem
(patch 0004). timespec_get is API 29+ and stays detected, otherwise Mesa's
c11 compat header redefines it and clashes with the NDK's declaration.
Adapted from Termux (which builds for API 24 and drops both).

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -228,7 +228,7 @@ foreach a : supported_function_attributes
   endif
 endforeach
 
-foreach f : ['memfd_create', 'strtok_r', 'timespec_get']
+foreach f : ['strtok_r', 'timespec_get']
   if cc.has_function(f)
     conf_data.set('HAVE_@0@'.format(f.to_upper()), 1)
   endif
